{
  // Phase 0 of the TypeScript adoption plan — see CLAUDE.md, "Engineering:
  // TypeScript adoption path" (Aug 14, 2026). JSDoc + checkJs only: no
  // .ts files, no build step, ever. Run with `npx tsc --noEmit` (or
  // `npm run typecheck`) — TypeScript became a real committed
  // devDependency (package.json) as of Phase 3 (Aug 16, 2026), see that
  // section below and esbuild.config.mjs.
  //
  // Scope is deliberately narrow — shared/*.js + gates-extended.js — same
  // scope the investigation behind this plan actually tested against, kept
  // low-risk on purpose. server.js and every tier's app.js are NOT covered
  // yet (untyped Express/Stripe/Supabase surface, much higher noise) — a
  // natural follow-up once Phase 0 proves out, not part of this pass.
  //
  // Mirrored into Tra (Aug 16, 2026, Tra PR #35) — Tra has its own
  // tsconfig.json/types.js, kept identical in the actual typedef bodies.
  //
  // Phase 1 ("shared contract types, hand-mirrored") is effectively the
  // same artifact as the mirror above — one shapes file, kept identical
  // across both repos — so it shipped together with the Tra mirror rather
  // than as a separate pass.
  //
  // Phase 2 (real .ts files, transpile-only, no bundler) picked up Aug 16,
  // 2026 — see tsconfig.build.json for the emit config. shared/types.js
  // (JSDoc) was replaced outright by shared/types.d.ts (real interfaces);
  // verified via a real tsc run with types.js removed that every existing
  // `@typedef {import('./types.js').X}` reference across gates-extended.js/
  // shared/*.js still resolves correctly against the .d.ts sibling with
  // zero new errors — standard TS Node-style resolution, not a guess.
  // shared/ticker-cache.ts is the first real .ts conversion (highest
  // fan-out leaf module — no internal shared/ dependencies, imported by 6
  // other files) — its compiled shared/ticker-cache.js is the actual
  // deploy artifact, committed alongside the .ts source.
  //
  // KNOWN, EXPECTED baseline noise on a fresh run (documented by the
  // investigation, not fixed by this pass):
  //   1. Every `./foo.js?v=N` import fails to resolve (TS2307) — the
  //      `?v=` cache-busting convention (see CLAUDE.md) isn't a valid
  //      module specifier to any resolver, tsc included. This is the
  //      concrete reason Phase 3 (a real bundler) is on the roadmap; not
  //      fixable here without breaking cache-busting.
  //   2. A handful of generic DOM-typing errors (`Property 'value' does
  //      not exist on type 'HTMLElement'`, `window.foo` assignments) from
  //      untyped `getElementById` call sites across shared/*.js predating
  //      this pass. Real but low-value churn to fully silence; left as
  //      known noise rather than casting every DOM access for this pass.
  // Neither category is a real bug — both were called out by name when
  // this plan was written. What Phase 0 actually adds is real @typedefs
  // (shared/types.d.ts) for the shapes that have shipped hidden bugs before
  // (GateResult / SectorContext / TickerData / the /analyze contract),
  // applied to gates-extended.js and shared/ticker-cache.ts/watchlist.js.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noImplicitAny": false,
    "strictNullChecks": false
  },
  "include": ["shared/*.js", "shared/*.ts", "shared/*.d.ts", "gates-extended.ts", "analyze-helpers.ts"]
}
